@*
    When external state was last read, and the deliberate act of reading it
    again.

    It is a component rather than a line inside the list because it appears
    without one — on a section header, beside a single reference, above a set of
    acts — and the rule it carries deserves one owner. That rule is: nothing in
    this product polls. State is read when somebody asks for it, so what is on
    screen is a reading with a time on it rather than a value that keeps itself
    true, and a surface that showed a state with no "as of" would be claiming a
    currency nothing here provides.

    The line is role="status" in every case, including a read that failed.
    .design/design-principles.md#local-first requires offline to be "a calm,
    persistent status — not an error modal", and a read that could not reach
    GitHub is the same class of thing: nothing broke, the network is simply not
    there. The one place this family escalates to role="alert" is an act that was
    invoked and failed, because that one is an event and it happened because the
    reader pressed something.
*@

<span class="@ClassValue" data-testid="@TestId">
    <span class="integration-freshness__text" role="status" data-testid="@TextTestId">@Line</span>

    @if (OnRefresh.HasDelegate)
    {
        <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.Ghost"
                   Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                   CssClass="integration-freshness__refresh"
                   Busy="@Reading.InFlight"
                   BusyLabel="@RefreshLabel"
                   TestId="@RefreshTestId"
                   OnClick="() => OnRefresh.InvokeAsync()">@RefreshLabel</AppButton>
    }
</span>

@code {
    [Parameter]
    public IntegrationReading Reading { get; set; } = IntegrationReading.Never;

    [Parameter]
    public string Prefix { get; set; } = "as of";

    [Parameter]
    public string NeverText { get; set; } = "Not checked yet";

    /// <summary>"Check now" rather than "Refresh". Refresh suggests something
    /// that would have happened anyway and is being hurried along; nothing here
    /// checks unless a person asks, and the label should not imply otherwise.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string RefreshLabel { get; set; } = "Check now";

    [Parameter]
    public IntegrationDensity Density { get; set; } = IntegrationDensity.Inline;

    /// <summary>Without a delegate there is no button, only the line. A surface
    /// that cannot re-read should not offer a control that would do nothing.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback OnRefresh { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string? CssClass { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string? TestId { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string? TextTestId { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string? RefreshTestId { get; set; }

    private string ClassValue
    {
        get
        {
            var stem = $"integration-freshness integration-freshness--{IntegrationStates.SlugOf(Density)}";
            return string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(CssClass) ? stem : $"{stem} {CssClass}";
        }
    }

    /// <summary>In flight first, then a failure, then the reading, then never.
    /// The order is the order a reader needs them: what is happening now beats
    /// what happened last, and "we tried and could not" beats a stale time that
    /// would read as current.</summary>
    private string Line
    {
        get
        {
            if (Reading.InFlight) return "Checking now…";

            if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Reading.FailureReason)) return $"Could not check — {Reading.FailureReason}";

            return string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Reading.AsOf) ? NeverText : $"{Prefix} {Reading.AsOf}";
        }
    }
}
